# SCENARIO: perceive_cross   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: auto
# Measurement: two hidden clients watching the same area must perceive the same effects. p1 stands
# in the Thais temple; an @cast camera rides a bot that is on p1's screen. merge.py's perception
# block reports, per ordered client pair, how many effects one client saw inside BOTH clients' core
# views (|dx|<=6, |dy|<=4) and how many of those the other client also saw (same id + tile, +-500 ms).
# The bot is paused (`/cavebot stop`, operator, undone by `resume` at the end) and p1 follows it,
# so the two views overlap for the whole hold. Also a creature/view
# sanity pass and the audio-off check on both clients (client-state).
@p1 login
@p1 goto 32367,32240,7 range=2 stuck=10
@p1 wait-see any-bot timeout=180 as=BOT
@cam:$BOT login
@srv cmd "$BOT" stop
@p1 client-state expect="audio_enabled=false"
@cam:$BOT client-state expect="audio_enabled=false"
@p1 perceive reset=1
@cam:$BOT perceive reset=1
@p1 wait-see $BOT timeout=20 optional=1
@p1 follow $BOT optional=1
@p1 hold 120 watch=$BOT
@p1 stop
@p1 view
@cam:$BOT view
@p1 perceive
@cam:$BOT perceive
@srv expect src=cli:p1 k=see_creature min=1
@srv expect src=cli:p1 k=see_effect min=1 optional=1
@srv expect-none src=cli:* k=tap_error
@srv cmd "$BOT" resume expect="resumed"
@cam:$BOT logout
@p1 logout
